EXAM_DATA.papers["2023-english-one"] = {"id":"2023-english-one","year":2023,"label":"2023 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2023-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Caravanserais were roadside inns that were built along the Silk Road in areas including China, North Africa and the Middle East. They were typically   {{1}}   outside the walls of a city or village and were usually funded by local governments or   {{2}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"The word \"caravanserai\" is a   {{3}}   of the Persian words \"karvan\", which means a group of travellers or a caravan, and \"saray\", a palace or enclosed building. The term caravan was used to   {{4}}   groups of people who travelled together across the ancient network for safety reasons,   {{5}}   merchants, travellers or pilgrims."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"From the 10th century onwards, as merchant and travel routes became more developed, the   {{6}}   of caravanserais increased and they served as a safe place for people to rest at night. Travellers on the Silk Road   {{7}}   the possibility of being attacked by thieves or being   {{8}}   to extreme weather conditions. For this reason, caravanserais were strategically placed   {{9}}   they could be reached in a day's travel time."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"Caravanserais served as an informal   {{10}}   point for the various people who travelled the Silk Road.   {{11}}   , these structures became important centres for cultural   {{12}}   and interaction, with travellers sharing their cultures, ideas and beliefs,   {{13}}   taking knowledge with them, greatly   {{14}}   the development of several civilisations."},{"id":"p-section1-5","text":"Caravanserais were also an important marketplace for commodities and   {{15}}   in the trade of goods along the Silk Road.   {{16}}   , it was frequently the first stop for merchants looking to sell their wares and   {{17}}   supplies for their own journeys. It is   {{18}}   that around 12,000 to 15,000 caravanserais were built along the Silk Road,   {{19}}   only about 3,000 are known to remain today, many of which are in   {{20}}   ."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"displayed"},{"key":"B","text":"occupied"},{"key":"C","text":"located"},{"key":"D","text":"equipped"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"线索是后接的方位短语 outside the walls were typically __(1)__ outside the walls of a city or village 中 outside the walls 是表\"地点\"的状语,要求空填一个能表\"(被)位于某处\"的动词,指向\"驿站坐落在城墙外\"这一空间事实。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"displayed 指陈列、展出,主语应是被展览之物,无法描述驿站\"坐落\"的位置。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"occupied 表\"占用/占领\",其被动 were occupied outside 不成立(occupy 后直接跟所占空间,不接 outside the walls 这种方位状语),搭配错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"located 与 outside the walls 构成 be located outside…(坐落于城墙之外),正是描述选址的标准说法,与下文\"由地方政府资助\"的客观介绍语气一致。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"equipped 指给…装备设施(be equipped with…),回答的是\"配了什么\",而非\"在哪里\",与方位状语 outside the walls 不对应。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"privately"},{"key":"B","text":"regularly"},{"key":"C","text":"respectively"},{"key":"D","text":"permanently"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"线索是并列项 local governments(政府=公共出资) funded by local governments or __(2)__ 提示两种出资来源并列:前者是\"政府(公共)\",空应表与之相对的另一来源。privately funded=私人出资,正好与\"政府出资\"形成公/私对照。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"privately funded 指由私人/民间资助,与 local governments(公共)由 or 并列,形成\"公或私\"两种来源,逻辑严丝合缝。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"regularly 描述时间频率,与前项\"政府\"(讲来源)不构成同一维度的对照,放入 or 并列后逻辑错位。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"respectively 表\"各自对应\",要求上文出现多组一一对应的列举,本句只有单一并列,无对应关系可言。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"permanently 表持续时长,同样不在\"由谁出资\"这一维度,与 governments 不形成来源对照。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"definition"},{"key":"B","text":"transition"},{"key":"C","text":"substitution"},{"key":"D","text":"combination"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"线索是 of … \"karvan\"… and \"saray\"(两个词相加) a __(3)__ of the Persian words \"karvan\"… and \"saray\" 把两个波斯词用 and 并提,且全段在讲该复合词的拆分,指向\"caravanserai 是两词的组合\"这一构词事实。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"definition 指释义,a definition of words 逻辑不通——caravanserai 不是对那两个词下定义,而是由它们拼成。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"transition 表从一种状态到另一种的转变,无法表达\"由 A 和 B 两个词组成\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"substitution 指用一个替代另一个,而本句是两词\"相加合成\"而非\"相互替换\",逻辑相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"combination 与 of … and … 完美搭配,意为 caravanserai 是 karvan 与 saray 两词的组合,正是下文逐词解释要支撑的结论。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"classify"},{"key":"B","text":"record"},{"key":"C","text":"describe"},{"key":"D","text":"connect"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"线索是主语\"The term caravan\"(一个称谓词) The term caravan was used to __(4)__ groups of people who travelled together across the ancient network 主语是一个术语,作用对象是\"结伴出行的人群\",指向\"这个词用来称呼/描述这群人\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"classify 指把对象分门别类,需有分类标准与多个类别;文中 caravan 只是统称一群人,并无分类动作。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"record 指记载存档,主语应是人或文献;一个称谓词无法\"记录\"人群,搭配不当。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"describe 与 The term…was used to 构成\"这个词用来描述/称呼…\"的标准说法,正好解释 caravan 一词的所指,符合词源段的客观说明语气。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"connect 表把事物联系起来;说一个术语\"连接结伴出行的人\"语义不通,偏离\"称呼\"这一核心。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"apart from"},{"key":"B","text":"instead of"},{"key":"C","text":"such as"},{"key":"D","text":"along with"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"5.","reason":"线索是 groups of people 与其后三类人的\"总—分\"关系 groups of people who travelled together across the ancient network for safety reasons, __(5)__ merchants, travellers or pilgrims:前为\"结伴出行的人群\"(总),后为商人、旅人、朝圣者(分),二者是\"整体—举例\"关系,要求 such as。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"apart from 表\"除去\",会把 merchants 等排除在\"人群\"之外,而文意是它们恰是人群的组成部分,逻辑相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"instead of 表\"取而代之\",意味用 merchants 替换 groups of people,但二者是包含关系而非替代关系。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"such as 用于列举前述概念的典型例子,merchants, travellers or pilgrims 正是 groups of people 的具体例子,搭配与逻辑双对。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"along with 表\"和…一起\",会把 merchants 等说成与\"人群\"并列的另一些人,而非人群的实例,层级关系错。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"construction"},{"key":"B","text":"restoration"},{"key":"C","text":"impression"},{"key":"D","text":"evaluation"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"线索是 routes became more developed → increased as merchant and travel routes became more developed, the __(6)__ of caravanserais increased:路线越发达,出行需求越大,自然\"修建\"的驿站数量增多,故空指向\"建造(construction)\"这一过程的增加。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"construction 指修建,the construction of caravanserais increased=驿站的修建增多,与 routes became more developed 的因果顺承一致。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"restoration 指修复已损坏的建筑;10世纪路线刚发达时是\"新建\"而非\"修旧\",语义偏。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"impression 表主观印象,无法被 routes developed 直接\"增多\",逻辑不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"evaluation 指评价、估值,与\"驿站随路线发达而变多\"的事实无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doubted"},{"key":"B","text":"faced"},{"key":"C","text":"accepted"},{"key":"D","text":"reduced"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"线索是宾语 the possibility of being attacked… extreme weather(纯负面风险) __(7)__ the possibility of being attacked by thieves or being __(8)__ to extreme weather:宾语全是出行风险,且下句 For this reason, caravanserais were strategically placed 说\"正因如此才(沿途)设驿站\",说明旅人是\"面临\"这些风险才需要驿站。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"doubted 表对其真实性存疑,但下文设驿站正说明风险确实存在,旅人不会\"怀疑\"它,逻辑相左。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"faced 指面对、面临,旅人面临被劫与恶劣天气的可能,与下句\"为此而设驿站\"的因果完全吻合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"accepted 含\"甘愿接受\"意味,但下文表明人们采取设驿站来\"规避\"风险,而非被动接受,色彩冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"reduced 指降低风险,但降低风险的是\"设驿站\"这一措施(下句),而非旅人在路上的动作,主谓逻辑错位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assigned"},{"key":"B","text":"subjected"},{"key":"C","text":"accustomed"},{"key":"D","text":"opposed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"线索是 being ___ to extreme weather 与前文 being attacked 并列(均为风险) being attacked by thieves or being __(8)__ to extreme weather conditions:由 or 与\"被劫\"并列,要求空也表一种被动遭受的负面处境;be subjected to=遭受、受制于,语义与之并列匹配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assigned to 表\"被分派给(某任务/某处)\",带不出\"遭受恶劣天气\"的意思,与并列项\"被劫\"的受害色彩不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"subjected 与 to 构成 be subjected to extreme weather=遭受恶劣天气,被动且负面,与 being attacked 并列,语义、搭配双对。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"accustomed to 表\"习惯于\",含中性甚至适应意味,而本处是旅人被迫遭受的风险,色彩冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"opposed to 表\"反对\",说旅人\"反对恶劣天气\"逻辑荒谬,且与\"被劫\"的被动遭受不并列。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so that"},{"key":"B","text":"even if"},{"key":"C","text":"now that"},{"key":"D","text":"in case"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"9.","reason":"线索是 strategically placed(有意为之)与\"一天可达\"的目的关系 were strategically placed __(9)__ they could be reached in a day's travel time:\"战略性地放置\"是手段,\"一天能到达\"是想达到的效果,二者是\"目的\"关系,需 so that(以便)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"so that 表目的,\"战略性选址\"正是\"为了能在一天内到达\",strategically 与目的状语呼应,逻辑最顺。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"even if 引出让步,但\"一天可达\"是选址追求的结果而非要克服的不利条件,无让步逻辑。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"now that 引已成立的原因,但\"一天可达\"是选址的目的(果),不是选址的前提(因),方向颠倒。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"in case 表\"以防万一(某不利情况)\",但\"被一天内到达\"是积极追求的目标而非要防范的风险,语义不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"talking"},{"key":"B","text":"starting"},{"key":"C","text":"breaking"},{"key":"D","text":"meeting"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"线索是 for the various people who travelled(各路人) an informal __(10)__ point for the various people who travelled the Silk Road:服务对象是\"各种各样在丝路上行走的人\",且下文讲他们\"分享文化、思想、信仰\",指向驿站是各路人\"相聚\"之地,meeting point=会合点。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"talking point 指\"谈资、话题\",是抽象议题而非供人聚集的场所,与 for the various people 的\"地点\"语义不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"starting point 指\"出发点/起点\",但驿站是沿途供\"各路人相聚交流\"之地,非旅程起始,且下文重在\"相会\"而非\"出发\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"breaking point 指\"临界/崩溃点\",带负面极限义,与\"非正式的人际汇聚地\"完全不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"meeting point 指\"碰头/会合地点\",与 for the various people 及下文\"分享文化、互相交流\"严丝合缝,是该段功能的核心定性。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By the way"},{"key":"B","text":"On occasion"},{"key":"C","text":"In comparison"},{"key":"D","text":"As a result"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"线索是上句\"会合点\"→本句\"成为文化交流中心\"的因果 上句 Caravanserais served as an informal __(10)__ point for the various people 说它是各路人汇聚地,本句 these structures became important centres for cultural __(12)__ and interaction 说由此成为文化交流中心——人聚集是因,成为交流中心是果,需 As a result。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"By the way 用于插入与主线无关的旁白,但本句是上句的直接结果、正是主线推进,语气不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"On occasion 表\"偶尔、间或\",但文中驿站\"成为重要文化中心\"是普遍稳定的结果,非偶发,程度范围不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"In comparison 需要前文有一可供比较的对象,但上句与本句是因果递进而非两者对照,缺对比基础。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"As a result 表因果,因驿站是各路人汇聚的会合点,\"结果\"它们成为文化交流的重要中心,逻辑顺承、衔接自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"heritage"},{"key":"B","text":"revival"},{"key":"C","text":"exchange"},{"key":"D","text":"status"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"线索是 with travellers sharing their cultures, ideas and beliefs(互相分享) cultural __(12)__ and interaction, with travellers sharing their cultures, ideas and beliefs:with 状语点明旅人\"彼此分享文化、思想、信仰\",这正是\"文化交流(exchange)\"的具体内容,与 interaction(互动)同义复现。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"heritage 指文化遗产,是被继承之物,无\"双向往来\"含义,与 interaction 及\"互相分享\"不同向。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"revival 指(文化的)复兴、重振,文中讲的是不同人之间\"互通\",而非某文化\"再度兴盛\",语义偏离。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"exchange 指交流、互换,cultural exchange 与 interaction 同向并列,正被 with travellers sharing… 这一\"互相分享\"具体化,严丝合缝。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"status 指地位、身份,既不与 interaction 同义,也与\"分享文化思想\"的行为无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"with regard to"},{"key":"B","text":"in spite of"},{"key":"C","text":"as well as"},{"key":"D","text":"in line with"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"13.","reason":"线索是\"sharing(分享出去)\"与\"taking knowledge(带走)\"两动作同向并列 sharing their cultures, ideas and beliefs, __(13)__ taking knowledge with them:旅人既\"分享自己的文化\"又\"带走(别人的)知识\",二者是旅人在驿站做的两件并行之事,属\"既…又…\"的并列,需 as well as。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"with regard to 表\"就…而言\",后接话题名词,无法把 sharing 与 taking 两个并行动作连成\"既…又…\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in spite of 表让步,要求前后矛盾;\"分享\"与\"带走知识\"是和谐并行的两件事,无对立,不能用让步。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"as well as 表\"以及、也\",自然把旅人\"分享文化\"与\"带走知识\"两件并行动作并列,正是文化交流\"有来有往\"的两面。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"in line with 表\"符合、按照\",后接标准/规定,无法连接两个并行的动作,语义不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"completing"},{"key":"B","text":"influencing"},{"key":"C","text":"resuming"},{"key":"D","text":"pioneering"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"线索是上文\"文化交流\"对\"文明发展\"的推动 travellers sharing their cultures… greatly __(14)__ the development of several civilisations:旅人在驿站交流文化的总效果,是\"极大地影响/推动了多个文明的发展\",故空指向 influencing(影响)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"completing 指使某事告竣,但\"文明的发展\"是持续进程,不能被\"完成\",且交流是促进而非终结发展。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"influencing 与 greatly 及宾语 the development 搭配,意为\"极大地影响了多个文明的发展\",正是文化交流的总体效果。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"resuming 指中断后重新开始,但文中文明发展并未中断,无\"恢复\"前提,语义不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"pioneering 指率先开创,宾语应是新领域/新事业,说\"开创文明的发展\"既搭配怪、又夸大了驿站的作用。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"aided"},{"key":"B","text":"invested"},{"key":"C","text":"failed"},{"key":"D","text":"competed"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"线索是 an important marketplace(重要市场,正面促进) Caravanserais were also an important marketplace for commodities and __(15)__ in the trade of goods:既是\"重要市场\",其对货物贸易自然是\"助力(aided)\",aid in=有助于,与\"市场\"的促进定位一致。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"aided 指帮助、促进,aided in the trade of goods=助力货物贸易,与前半句\"是重要市场\"的正面促进作用一致,搭配 aid in 也成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"invested in 指投资,主语应是人/机构;说驿站(场所)\"投资于货物贸易\"主体不当,且与\"市场\"的中介促进作用不同。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"failed 表失败,与前半句肯定驿站\"是重要市场\"的褒义定调正相反,色彩冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"competed in 表参与竞争,但驿站是供交易的场所、起促进作用,不是与人争利的竞争者,逻辑不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Rather"},{"key":"B","text":"Indeed"},{"key":"C","text":"Otherwise"},{"key":"D","text":"However"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"16.","reason":"线索是上句\"重要市场\"与本句\"常是商人第一站\"的同向强化 上句 Caravanserais were also an important marketplace 说它是重要市场,本句 it was frequently the first stop for merchants looking to sell their wares 进一步举证它常是商人卖货的第一站——后者是对前者的强化印证,需 Indeed(的确)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Rather 表\"(不是…)而是…\",要求前面有被否定的说法;上句是肯定陈述,无需纠正,逻辑不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Indeed 表\"的确、确实\",本句用\"常是商人卖货第一站\"进一步坐实上句\"是重要市场\",同向强化,衔接自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Otherwise 表\"要不然(会怎样)\",引出相反假设结果;本句是顺承事实陈述,无假设逻辑。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"However 表转折,要求前后语义相反;此处本句与上句同向(都讲它的市场/贸易作用),无转折,误用会割裂逻辑。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"go in for"},{"key":"B","text":"stand up for"},{"key":"C","text":"close in on"},{"key":"D","text":"stock up on"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"17.","reason":"线索是 supplies for their own journeys(为自己旅途备的物资) sell their wares and __(17)__ supplies for their own journeys:商人来此既卖货(sell wares)又为自己旅程\"备足补给\",stock up on=囤积、大量购入,与 supplies 及\"备旅途之需\"完全契合。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"go in for 表\"从事、热衷于(某活动)\",宾语应是活动/爱好,接 supplies(物资)语义不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"stand up for 表\"为…挺身而出、维护\",宾语应是权利/人/立场,与\"备物资\"无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"close in on 表\"逼近、围拢(目标)\",带追捕意味,与\"购备补给\"毫无关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"stock up on 指大量购入囤积,stock up on supplies for their own journeys=为自己的旅程备足补给,搭配与语义双对,与 sell wares 并列也自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"believed"},{"key":"B","text":"predicted"},{"key":"C","text":"recalled"},{"key":"D","text":"implied"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"线索是\"around 12,000 to 15,000…were built\"(对过去数量的估算) It is __(18)__ that around 12,000 to 15,000 caravanserais were built along the Silk Road:around、to 表明这是对历史建造数量的\"估算/据信\",而非预测未来、回忆或暗示,指向 believed(据信)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"believed 用于 It is believed that(人们据信/普遍认为),引出对过去建造数量的概略估计,客观中立,与说明文语气和 around…to… 的不确定数字契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"predicted 用于预测将来之事,但从句 were built 是已发生的历史,无法\"预测\"过去,时间逻辑矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"recalled 表回忆,主体应是经历过的人;千年前的建造数量无人亲历可\"回忆\",且 It is recalled that 不是表客观估计的惯用结构。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"implied 表含蓄暗示,但本句是直接、明确地给出估算数字,并非\"言外之意\",语义不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"until"},{"key":"B","text":"because"},{"key":"C","text":"unless"},{"key":"D","text":"although"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"19.","reason":"线索是\"建过 12,000-15,000\"与\"今仅存约 3,000\"的数量反差 around 12,000 to 15,000… were built…, __(19)__ only about 3,000 are known to remain today:曾建上万座 vs 今仅存约三千座,数字\"多\"与\"少\"形成鲜明反差(尤其 only 强化),属转折,需 although(尽管/虽然)。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"until 表\"直到某时\",但两分句是\"建造总数\"与\"现存数\"的数量对比,非\"持续到某时\"的时间关系。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"because 表原因,但\"曾建很多\"不是\"今存很少\"的原因(存得少另有损毁原因),强加因果不成立。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"unless 引出条件,但两分句都是既成事实的陈述,无\"条件—结果\"关系,逻辑不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"although 表\"尽管、虽然\",引出与前句相反的事实:虽曾建一两万座,如今却仅约3000座存留,only 强化了这一让步转折,逻辑最贴。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ruins"},{"key":"B","text":"debt"},{"key":"C","text":"fashion"},{"key":"D","text":"series"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"20.","reason":"线索是 only about 3,000 remain(幸存的古老建筑) only about 3,000 are known to remain today, many of which are in __(20)__:主语是\"今天仅存的约3000座古驿站\",其中许多\"年久失修\",in ruins=破败、成废墟,与古迹存留至今的破损现状契合。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"ruins 与 in 构成 in ruins(破败、残破不堪),恰好描述这些历经千年、许多已残破的幸存驿站,收束全篇\"如今仅存且多已破败\"的现状。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"debt 的 in debt 指负债,主语应是有经济行为的人或机构,建筑物不会\"负债\",主体不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"fashion 的 in fashion 表\"时兴、流行\",与古老幸存且多已残破的驿站现状色彩完全相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"series 的 in series 多指(电路)串联或\"成系列\",描述建筑保存状态不通,语义不搭。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"The weather in Texas may have cooled since the recent extreme heat, but the temperature will be high at the State Board of Education meeting in Austin this month as officials debate how climate change is taught in Texas schools."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Pat Hardy, who sympathises with the views of the energy sector, is resisting proposed changes to science standards for pre-teen pupils. \"There are as many scientists working against all the panic of global climate change as there are those who are pushing it,\" she claims. \"Texas is an energy state and we need to recognise that. You need to remember where your bread is buttered.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"Most scientists and experts sharply dispute Hardy's views. Board members like her \"casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists as just another misguided opinion,\" says Dan Quinn, senior communications strategist at the Texas Freedom Network, a non-profit group that monitors public education."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Such debates reflect fierce discussions across the US, as researchers, policymakers, teachers and students step up demands for a greater focus on teaching about the facts of climate change in schools."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"A study last year by the National Center for Science Education, a non-profit group of scientists and teachers, looking at how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes, gave barely half of US states a grade B+ or higher. Among the 10 worst performers were some of the most populous states, including Texas, which was given the lowest grade (F) and has a disproportionate influence because its textbooks are widely sold elsewhere."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"Glenn Branch, the centre's deputy director, cautions that setting state-level science standards is only one limited benchmark in a country that decentralises decisions to local school boards. Even if a state is considered a high performer in its science standards, \"that does not mean it will be taught\", he says."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-7","text":"Another issue is that while climate change is well integrated into some subjects and at some ages—such as earth and space sciences in high schools—it is not as well represented in curricula for younger children and in subjects that are more widely taught, such as biology and chemistry. It is also less prominent in many social studies courses."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-8","text":"Branch points out that, even if a growing number of official guidelines and textbooks reflect scientific consensus on climate change, unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers. They include materials sponsored by energy industry associations."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"In Paragraph 1, the weather in Texas is mentioned to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"forecast a policy shift in Texas schools."},{"key":"B","text":"stress the consequences of climate change."},{"key":"C","text":"indicate the atmosphere at the board meeting."},{"key":"D","text":"draw the public's attention to energy shortages."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"第1段中提到德克萨斯州的天气是为了","choicesZh":{"A":"预测德克萨斯州学校的政策转变。","B":"强调气候变化的后果。","C":"表明董事会会议的气氛。","D":"引起公众对能源短缺的关注。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干用 the weather in Texas is mentioned to，问的是「提到 weather 是为了……」——这是典型的写作意图/例证目的设问，而不是细节核对。","parse":"In Paragraph 1, the weather in Texas is mentioned to 是一个被动语态加不定式的不完整陈述句，骨架为「the weather is mentioned (in order) to do sth」，四个选项均为不定式短语，是该不完整句的尾巴；in order 被省略，但 to 引出的仍是目的状语，理解时把 mentioned to 还原成「提到 X 的目的是……」即可，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The weather in Texas may have cooled since the recent extreme heat, but the temperature will be high at the State Board of Education meeting in Austin this month as officials debate how climate change is taught in Texas schools.","locateZh":"Texas 的天气在近期极端高温之后或许已经降温，但本月在 Austin 召开的州教育委员会会议上，「气温」却会很高——因为官员们将就气候变化如何在 Texas 学校中被教授一事展开辩论。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"forecast a policy shift in Texas schools 中的 policy shift 在第 1 段并无任何支撑——原文只说会议将「辩论 how climate change is taught」，辩论本身既未给出政策走向，也未预告任何 shift。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"stress the consequences of climate change 把题目从「为什么提天气」答成了「天气是气候变化的后果」——第 1 段提天气是为了双关会议气氛，并未把 the recent extreme heat 用来强调气候变化的后果。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是「类比烘托会议气氛」，indicate the atmosphere at the board meeting 中的 indicate + atmosphere + board meeting 三处分别对接「烘托」「气氛」「教委会」——三角全中，C 项即为正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"the temperature will be high at the State Board of Education meeting","opt":"indicate the atmosphere at the board meeting"},{"orig":"officials debate how climate change is taught in Texas schools","opt":"atmosphere at the board meeting"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"draw the public's attention to energy shortages 中的 energy shortages 在第 1 段没有任何对应——首段谈 climate change is taught，从未提及能源短缺；公众的注意力也并非段落主语关心的对象。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"What does Quinn think of Hardy?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"She exaggerates the existing panic."},{"key":"B","text":"She denies the value of scientific work."},{"key":"C","text":"She shows no concern for pre-teens."},{"key":"D","text":"She expresses self-contradictory views."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Quinn 如何看待 Hardy?","choicesZh":{"A":"她夸大了现有的恐慌。","B":"她否认科学工作的价值。","C":"她对青春期前儿童毫不关心。","D":"她表达了自相矛盾的观点。"},"analysis":{"type":"What does Quinn think of Hardy? 问 Quinn 对 Hardy 的具体看法，定位句中即有原话，属于客观转述细节，不必跨段推理。","parse":"What does Quinn think of Hardy? 是 think of sb 的常规疑问句式，think of = have an opinion of，无倒装无省略，骨架透明。","locateEn":"Most scientists and experts sharply dispute Hardy's views. Board members like her \"casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists as just another misguided opinion,\" says Dan Quinn, senior communications strategist at the Texas Freedom Network, a non-profit group that monitors public education.","locateZh":"大多数科学家和专家强烈反对 Hardy 的观点。Texas Freedom Network 高级传播策略师 Dan Quinn 说，像她这样的董事会成员「将学者和科学家的毕生工作随随便便地当作又一个被误导的观点而不予理睬」。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"exaggerates the existing panic 与原文不符——Quinn 并未指控 Hardy 夸大 panic；恰恰相反，是 Hardy 自己在第 2 段把 all the panic of global climate change 当作被反对的对象，Quinn 评价她的是「轻视学者」而非「夸大恐慌」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判核心是「Hardy 轻视、否定科研工作价值」，She denies the value of scientific work 中 denies + value + scientific work 三项分别对接「否定」「价值」「科研工作」——完全咬合，B 项即为正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists","opt":"denies the value of scientific work"},{"orig":"as just another misguided opinion","opt":"denies the value"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"shows no concern for pre-teens 凭空生造「不关心未成年学生」这一论点——第 3 段 Quinn 的评价只涉及对待「学者和科学家的研究工作」，从未谈到 Hardy 对 pre-teens 的态度。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"expresses self-contradictory views 指责 Hardy 「自相矛盾」——第 3 段 Quinn 只批评她「轻视学者」，并未指出她观点内部存在矛盾；考生回原文找不到任何 contradict / contradictory 的同义表达。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The study mentioned in Paragraph 5 shows that","options":[{"key":"A","text":"climate education is insufficient at state public schools."},{"key":"B","text":"policymakers have little drive for science education."},{"key":"C","text":"Texas is reluctant to rewrite its science textbooks."},{"key":"D","text":"environmental teaching in some states lacks supervision."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第5段提到的研究表明","choicesZh":{"A":"州立公立学校的气候教育不足。","B":"政策制定者对科学教育缺乏动力。","C":"德克萨斯州不愿重写其科学教科书。","D":"一些州的环境教学缺乏监督。"},"analysis":{"type":"The study mentioned in Paragraph 5 shows that 让你转述该研究「表明了什么」，是对研究结论的客观复述，归入细节题。","parse":"The study mentioned in Paragraph 5 shows that 中 mentioned in Paragraph 5 是过去分词短语后置修饰 study，shows 是真正谓语；选项是 that 引导的宾语从句的内容，理解时记住主语是「研究」、动作是「shows（表明）」即可，无陷阱。","locateEn":"A study last year by the National Center for Science Education, a non-profit group of scientists and teachers, looking at how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes, gave barely half of US states a grade B+ or higher.","locateZh":"去年由 National Center for Science Education（一个由科学家与教师组成的非营利组织）开展的一项研究——该研究考察全美各州公立学校如何在科学课上处理气候变化——只给将将一半的美国州打出了 B+ 或更高的等级。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求「全美一半多州气候教育不达标」三层信息——研究对象（state public schools）、研究内容（climate education）、研究结论（insufficient）——A 项 climate education is insufficient at state public schools 三层全中、无延伸，是正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"gave barely half of US states a grade B+ or higher","opt":"climate education is insufficient at state public schools"},{"orig":"state public schools across the country","opt":"state public schools"},{"orig":"how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes","opt":"climate education"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"policymakers have little drive for science education 把研究结论的对象换成了「政策制定者」，但研究考察的是 state public schools 的教育成效，未涉及政策制定者的驱动力。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Texas is reluctant to rewrite its science textbooks 把研究的全美结论窄化为 Texas 的具体行为；原文虽提到 Texas, which was given the lowest grade (F)，但只说 Texas 评级最低、并未说 Texas「不愿意改写教材」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"environmental teaching in some states lacks supervision 中的 supervision（监管）在原文研究段没有任何对应——研究只评分，未谈监管缺失；environmental 与 climate 也并非等价改写，前者范围更广。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"According to Branch, state-level science standards in the US______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"call for regular revision."},{"key":"B","text":"require urgent application."},{"key":"C","text":"have limited influence."},{"key":"D","text":"cater to local needs."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据 Branch 的说法,美国州级科学标准","choicesZh":{"A":"需要定期修订。","B":"需要紧急应用。","C":"影响有限。","D":"迎合地方需求。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to Branch, state-level science standards in the US 让你转述 Branch 关于 state-level science standards 的原话，答案直接在他的话里，无需推断。","parse":"According to Branch, state-level science standards in the US 是带空格的不完整陈述句，According to Branch 作插入语，state-level science standards 是主语，in the US 后置修饰主语，谓语和宾语藏在四个选项里；理解时把 Branch 的原话补到空白处对比即可，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Glenn Branch, the centre's deputy director, cautions that setting state-level science standards is only one limited benchmark in a country that decentralises decisions to local school boards.","locateZh":"该中心的副主任 Glenn Branch 提醒说，在一个把决策权下放给地方学区的国家里，制定州一级的科学标准只是一个有限的参照指标。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"call for regular revision 在第 6 段没有任何支撑——Branch 只评价州级标准的影响是有限的，从未谈到「需要定期修订」；regular revision 是凭空生造的新论点。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"require urgent application 强调「亟需推行/应用」，但 Branch 的态度是「州级标准是 only one limited benchmark」——他在弱化、降级而不是催促紧急推行，方向恰好相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判核心「州级标准影响力有限」由 limited 与 decentralises 两点共同支撑，have limited influence 中 limited 直接同根复用、influence 与 benchmark 在「指标→实际作用」上等值——双重锁定，C 即为正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"only one limited benchmark","opt":"have limited influence"},{"orig":"in a country that decentralises decisions to local school boards","opt":"limited"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"cater to local needs 把「决策权下放给地方学区」偷换成「迎合地方需要」——Branch 的本意是「正因为下放，所以州级标准影响有限」，他既未说州级标准 cater to local needs，也未表态州级标准要去迎合地方。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"It is implied in the last paragraph that climate change teaching in some schools______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"agrees to major public demands."},{"key":"B","text":"reflects teachers' personal bias."},{"key":"C","text":"may misrepresent the energy sector."},{"key":"D","text":"can be swayed by external forces."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"最后一段暗示一些学校的气候变化教学","choicesZh":{"A":"符合主要公众需求。","B":"反映了教师的个人偏见。","C":"可能歪曲了能源行业。","D":"可能受到外部力量的影响。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 It is implied in the last paragraph that 中的 implied 直接亮出推断属性——答案是末段字面信息的一步合理延伸，而不是逐字复现。","parse":"It is implied in the last paragraph that climate change teaching in some schools 是 It 形式主语句式，真正的主语从句由 that 引导，从句主语是 climate change teaching in some schools，谓语和补足成分藏在四个选项里；in some schools 是关键限定，提醒考生答案只指向「部分」而非全部学校，无陷阱但需留心范围词。","locateEn":"Branch points out that, even if a growing number of official guidelines and textbooks reflect scientific consensus on climate change, unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers. They include materials sponsored by energy industry associations.","locateZh":"Branch 指出，即便越来越多的官方指南和教材反映了气候变化的科学共识，仍有一些非官方教育资料正被分发给老师，这些资料传递的是更具偏向性的观点。其中包括由能源行业协会赞助的材料。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"agrees to major public demands 中的 public demands 在末段没有任何对应——Branch 强调的是「非官方资料正在影响教学」，并未说教学迎合了公众诉求；甚至与第 4 段提到 fierce discussions 的公众呼声相比，本段呈现的是相反方向：教学被行业利益渗透而非顺应公众诉求。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"reflects teachers' personal bias 把责任推到「老师本人有偏见」——但末段 unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers 说的是资料被分发给老师，老师是受方而非来源，slanted（偏向性）形容的是资料，不是老师本人。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"may misrepresent the energy sector 暗示教学「歪曲了能源行业」——但末段说的是 materials sponsored by energy industry associations，即能源行业资助资料去影响教学；是行业在「输出叙事」，而不是学校在「歪曲行业」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判核心是「部分学校的气候教学被非官方/外部力量影响」，can be swayed by external forces 用 can 控住语气、用 swayed 等值 distributed/influenced、用 external forces 抽象 energy industry associations——一步推断、不增不减，D 项即为正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers","opt":"can be swayed by external forces"},{"orig":"materials sponsored by energy industry associations","opt":"external forces"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Communities throughout New England have been attempting to regulate short-term rentals since sites like Airbnb took off in the 2010s. Now, with record-high home prices and historically low inventory, there's an increased urgency in such regulation, particularly among those who worry that developers will come in and buy up swaths of housing to flip for a fortune on the short-term rental market."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"In New Hampshire, where the rental vacancy rate has dropped below 1 percent, housing advocates fear unchecked short-term rentals will put further pressure on an already strained market. The state Legislature recently voted against a bill that would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"\"We are at a crisis level on the supply of rental housing,\" said Nick Taylor, executive director of the Workforce Housing Coalition of the Greater Seacoast. Without enough affordable housing in southern New Hampshire towns, \"employers are having a hard time attracting employees, and workers are having a hard time finding a place to live,\" Taylor said."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"However, short-term rentals also provide housing for tourists, pointed out Ryan Castle, CEO of a local association of realtors. \"A lot of workers are servicing the tourist industry, and the tourism industry is serviced by those people coming in short term,\" Castle said, \"and so it's a cyclical effect.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Short-term rentals themselves are not the crux of the issue, said Keren Hom, an expert on affordable housing policy. \"I think individuals being able to rent out their second home is a good thing. If it's their vacation home anyway, and it's just empty, why can't you make money off it?\" Hom said. Issues arise, however, when developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities—de facto hotels—to bypass taxes and regulations. \"I think the question is, shouldn't a developer who's really building a hotel, but disguising it as not a hotel, be treated and taxed and regulated like a hotel?\" Hom said."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"At the end of 2018, Governor Charlie Baker of Massachusetts signed a bill to rein in those potential investor-buyers. The bill requires every rental host to register with the state, mandates they carry insurance, and opens the potential for local taxes on top of a new state levy. Boston took things even further, requiring renters to register with the city's Inspectional Services Department."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-7","text":"Hom said similar registration requirements could benefit struggling cities and towns, but \"if we want to make a change in the housing market, the main one is we have to build a lot more.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Which of the following is true of New England?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Its housing supply is at a very low level."},{"key":"B","text":"Its communities are in need of funding."},{"key":"C","text":"Its rental vacancy rate is going up slowly."},{"key":"D","text":"Its home prices are under strict control."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于新英格兰,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"其住房供应处于非常低的水平。","B":"其社区需要资金支持。","C":"其租赁空置率正在缓慢上升。","D":"其房价受到严格控制。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of New England 没有给出具体细节方向，只问 \"哪个对\"，须把四个选项当四道小细节题逐一回原文核对。","parse":"题干 Which of the following is true of New England? 是一个直接特殊疑问句，主干 Which is true，of New England 是后置介词短语限定话题范围。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Now, with record-high home prices and historically low inventory, there's an increased urgency in such regulation, particularly among those who worry that developers will come in and buy up swaths of housing to flip for a fortune on the short-term rental market.","locateZh":"如今，由于房价创历史新高、库存处于历史低位，对此类监管的紧迫性进一步上升，尤其是那些担心开发商进场扫货、把大批房源翻新后投放短租市场牟利的人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 A 与 historically low inventory 一一对应，其余三项与原文要么相反要么无据。","pairs":[{"orig":"historically low inventory","opt":"housing supply is at a very low level"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"in need of funding（缺资金）与原文焦点 record-high home prices and historically low inventory 不在同一维度，原文从头到尾未谈社区资金问题。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说 rental vacancy rate has dropped below 1 percent（空置率下降），选项却说 going up slowly（缓慢上升），方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 record-high home prices 表明房价创新高、无任何被控制的描述，选项 under strict control 凭空生成 \"严格控制\" 的状态。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"The bill mentioned in Paragraph 2 was intended to______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"curb short-term rental speculation."},{"key":"B","text":"ensure the supply of cheap housing."},{"key":"C","text":"punish illegal dealings in housing."},{"key":"D","text":"allow a free short-term rental market."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第2段中提到的法案旨在______","choicesZh":{"A":"遏制短期租赁投机行为。","B":"确保廉价住房的供应。","C":"惩罚非法住房交易。","D":"允许自由的短期租赁市场。"},"analysis":{"type":"was intended to 询问议案的具体意图，正确答案应是原文议案描述的客观转述。","parse":"题干为不完整陈述句 The bill mentioned in Paragraph 2 was intended to______。主语 The bill，定语 mentioned in Paragraph 2 是过去分词后置定语，谓语 was intended to 接选项作补足。需要特别警惕的是：原文第 2 段说 voted against a bill that would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals，这里既有 against（反对），又有 illegal（禁止），又有 restricting（限制）三重否定/限制叠加，理清议案本身的 intend 是关键。","locateEn":"The state Legislature recently voted against a bill that would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals.","locateZh":"州议会最近投票否决了一项原本会使各镇制定限制短租之法规变为违法的议案。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"curb short-term rental speculation 是 \"遏制短租投机\"，而议案本意是阻止地方限制短租，方向恰好相反。考生若没看出 made it illegal+restricting 的双否定，就会被 short-term rental 这个共有词带跑。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"议案本身只关于地方能否立法限制短租，并没有提及保障廉租房供给。ensure the supply of cheap housing 是 Taylor 在第 3 段的诉求，与本议案目的张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"议案涉及的是各镇能否制定限制法规，与 punish illegal dealings in housing 所说的 \"惩治非法房产交易\" 完全无关，原文也没有 illegal dealings 的概念。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"议案的意图是禁止地方限制短租，等价于保留短租市场的自由，正与 D 项 allow a free short-term rental market 等值。","pairs":[{"orig":"made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals","opt":"allow a free short-term rental market"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"Compared with Castle, Taylor is more likely to support______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"further investment in local tourism."},{"key":"B","text":"an increase in affordable housing."},{"key":"C","text":"strict management of real estate agents."},{"key":"D","text":"a favorable policy for short-term workers."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"与Castle相比,Taylor更可能支持______","choicesZh":{"A":"进一步投资当地旅游业。","B":"增加经济适用房。","C":"对房地产经纪人进行严格管理。","D":"对短期工作者实施优惠政策。"},"analysis":{"type":"is more likely to support 是基于人物立场的一步外推，要从 Taylor 的发言推他更可能支持的政策方向。","parse":"题干 Compared with Castle, Taylor is more likely to support______ 是不完整陈述句。Compared with Castle 是分词短语作状语，逻辑主语是 Taylor；主干 Taylor is more likely to support…。关键短语 more likely to 表外推语气——答案是 Taylor 立场的一步合理延伸，而非原文原话。","locateEn":"\"We are at a crisis level on the supply of rental housing,\" said Nick Taylor, executive director of the Workforce Housing Coalition of the Greater Seacoast. Without enough affordable housing in southern New Hampshire towns, \"employers are having a hard time attracting employees, and workers are having a hard time finding a place to live,\" Taylor said.","locateZh":"\"我们的租赁房屋供给已到危机水平，\" 大海岸地区劳动力住房联盟执行主任 Nick Taylor 说。在新罕布什尔南部各镇缺乏足够可负担房屋的情况下，\"雇主很难吸引到员工，工人也很难找到住处，\" Taylor 说。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"further investment in local tourism 完全是 Castle 的角度（旅游业-工人-短租循环），不是 Taylor 的诉求。Taylor 关心的是住房供给。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四项里只有 B 抓住 Taylor 反复点名的 affordable housing 焦点；其余三项要么属于 Castle（旅游）要么偏题（房地产代理/短期工人）。","pairs":[{"orig":"Without enough affordable housing in southern New Hampshire towns","opt":"an increase in affordable housing"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Taylor 没有提及房地产中介；管理 real estate agents 这一诉求原文无任何依据。原文里的 realtors 出现在 Ryan Castle, CEO of a local association of realtors，是 Castle 的身份描述，并非 Taylor 主张要管的对象。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Taylor 关心的是 employees / workers 找不到住处，而非 a favorable policy for short-term workers（针对短期工人的政策）。原文 those people coming in short term 出自 Castle 之口，描述旅游产业的短期客群，与 Taylor 关切的本地工人立场不同。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"What does Hom emphasize in Paragraph 5?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The urgency to upgrade short-term rental facilities."},{"key":"B","text":"The efficient operation of the local housing market."},{"key":"C","text":"The necessity to stop developers from evading taxes."},{"key":"D","text":"The proper procedures for renting out spare houses."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Hom在第5段中强调了什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"升级短期租赁设施的紧迫性。","B":"当地住房市场的高效运作。","C":"阻止开发商逃税的必要性。","D":"出租闲置房屋的正当程序。"},"analysis":{"type":"What does Hom emphasize in Paragraph 5 是对第 5 段 Hom 发言重心的客观核对，重心句即考点句。","parse":"题干 What does Hom emphasize in Paragraph 5? 是一个一般疑问句结构，What 作 emphasize 的宾语前置，主语 Hom，谓语 emphasize，状语 in Paragraph 5。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Issues arise, however, when developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities—de facto hotels—to bypass taxes and regulations. \"I think the question is, shouldn't a developer who's really building a hotel, but disguising it as not a hotel, be treated and taxed and regulated like a hotel?\" Hom said.","locateZh":"然而，当开发商企图建造大规模短租设施（实质上的酒店）以绕开税收和监管时，问题就出现了。\"我想问题是：开发商实际上在建酒店，却把它伪装成非酒店，他难道不该像酒店那样被对待、被征税、被监管吗？\" Hom 说。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Hom 没有谈及短租设施的硬件升级问题，upgrade short-term rental facilities 是凭空捏造的诉求。原文出现的 short-term rental facilities 字样只是被她用来批评 \"开发商伪装酒店\"，不是要升级它。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Hom 在第 5 段强调的是堵漏（监管和征税），不是市场的高效运转。efficient operation of the local housing market 是宏观、空泛的概念，原文无对应。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Hom 全段的真正强调由 however 引出、由反问句收尾，焦点是 \"阻止开发商以伪装方式避税\"，C 项与之精准吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities—de facto hotels—to bypass taxes and regulations","opt":"The necessity to stop developers from evading taxes"},{"orig":"shouldn't a developer who's really building a hotel, but disguising it as not a hotel, be treated and taxed and regulated like a hotel","opt":"stop developers from evading taxes"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"proper procedures for renting out spare houses 把 Hom 的强调降级为 \"个人闲置房出租的程序\"。原文中她确实说过 individuals being able to rent out their second home is a good thing，但这是让步的铺垫，而非 emphasize 的对象。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"Hom holds that imposing registration requirements is______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"an irrational decision."},{"key":"B","text":"an unfeasible proposal."},{"key":"C","text":"an unnecessary measure."},{"key":"D","text":"an inadequate solution."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Hom认为实施登记要求是______","choicesZh":{"A":"一项不合理的决定。","B":"一项不可行的提议。","C":"一项不必要的措施。","D":"一项不充分的解决方案。"},"analysis":{"type":"Hom holds that 配合让步结构 could benefit … but if we want to make a change … we have to build a lot more，正确答案是从 \"but\" 转折推出的态度判断。","parse":"题干 Hom holds that imposing registration requirements is______ 是不完整陈述句。主语 Hom，谓语 holds that 接宾语从句；从句主语 imposing registration requirements 是动名词短语作主语，谓语 is 后接选项形容词短语作表语。要点是动名词 imposing 把第 6 段那种 \"强制登记\" 的政策名词化，问 Hom 对它的总体评价。","locateEn":"Hom said similar registration requirements could benefit struggling cities and towns, but \"if we want to make a change in the housing market, the main one is we have to build a lot more.\"","locateZh":"Hom 表示，类似的登记要求或许能让陷入困境的城镇受益，但 \"如果我们真想改变住房市场，最关键的一件事是我们必须多建房。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"an irrational decision 意为 \"不理智的决定\"，否定彻底。但 Hom 明明承认登记 could benefit struggling cities and towns，并未否定其合理性，仅认为它不够。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"an unfeasible proposal（不可行的提议）涉及 \"能否实施\" 的维度，Hom 全文没讨论登记是否可行，而是讨论它够不够。原文 P6 提到马萨诸塞已实施类似政策，反而证明可行。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"an unnecessary measure 等于完全否定登记的必要性，但原文 could benefit struggling cities and towns 明确承认它有用，本身就证明它并非 unnecessary。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Hom 既不否认登记的部分价值，又点明真正的解药是多建房；D 项 an inadequate solution 完整保留这两层语义——它仍是 solution（承认有用），但是 inadequate（不充分）。","pairs":[{"orig":"could benefit struggling cities and towns, but \"if we want to make a change in the housing market, the main one is we have to build a lot more\"","opt":"an inadequate solution"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"If you're heading for your nearest branch of Waterstones, the biggest book retailer in the UK, in search of the Duchess of Sussex's new children's book The Bench, you might have to be prepared to hunt around a bit; the same may be true of The President's Daughter, the new thriller by Bill Clinton and James Patterson. Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House (PRH), a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The problem began late last year, when PRH confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones \"at a very significant level\". The trade magazine The Bookseller reported that Waterstones branch managers were being told to remove PRH books from prominent areas such as tables, display spaces and windows, and were \"quietly retiring them to their relevant sections\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"PRH declined to comment on the issue, but a spokesperson for Waterstones told me: \"Waterstones are currently operating with reduced credit terms from PRH, the only publisher in the UK to place any limitations on our ability to trade. We are not boycotting PRH titles but we are doing our utmost to ensure that availability for customers remains good despite the lower overall levels of stock. We are hopeful with our shops now open again that normality will return and that we will be allowed to buy appropriately. Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"In the meantime, PRH authors have been the losers. Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"It comes at a time when authors are already worried about the consequences of the proposed merger between PRH and another big publisher, Simon & Schuster—the reduction in the number of unaligned UK publishers is likely to lead to fewer bidding wars, lower advances, and more conformity in terms of what is published."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"\"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power,\" says literary agent Andrew Lownie. \"The publishing industry talks about diversity in terms of authors and staff but it also needs a plurality of ways of delivering intellectual contact, choice and different voices. After all, many of the most interesting books in recent years have come from small publishers.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-7","text":"We shall see whether that plurality is a casualty of the current need among publishers to be big enough to take on all-comers."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The author mentions two books in Paragraph 1 to present______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"an ongoing conflict."},{"key":"B","text":"an intellectual concept."},{"key":"C","text":"a prevailing sentiment."},{"key":"D","text":"a literary phenomenon."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者在第一段提到两本书是为了呈现______","choicesZh":{"A":"一种持续的冲突。","B":"一个知识概念。","C":"一种普遍的情绪。","D":"一种文学现象。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author mentions two books in Paragraph 1 to present，主句结构\"作者举例 + to present + 名词\"——是典型的\"举例服务于何种主张\"句式。","parse":"主干 The author mentions two books，in Paragraph 1 作地点状语；to present 是目的状语，后接选项里的名词短语。结构平铺直叙、无陷阱，只需看清\"to present\"问的是\"提及的目的\"。","locateEn":"Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House (PRH), a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones.","locateZh":"这两本书都将由企鹅兰登（PRH）在下周出版，而该公司目前正与 Waterstones 处于僵持状态。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"举两本书是\"现象\"，紧随其后的 stand-off 句把现象升格为论点——这个论点的语义中心是\"两家正陷在持续的对抗里\"，与 an ongoing conflict 完全等值。","pairs":[{"orig":"a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones","opt":"an ongoing conflict"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"an intellectual concept 指\"思想/学术概念\"——第 1 段从书名到段尾全是商业/销售层面的现象，毫无任何\"理念/学说\"的元素。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a prevailing sentiment 指\"流行的情绪/情感\"——原文谈的是两家公司之间的商业僵持，不是公众情绪；sentiment 把\"对峙\"偷换成了\"普遍情感\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"a literary phenomenon 把两本书拔高为\"一种文学现象\"——原文只是用两本具体新书作为商业争端的载体，并未讨论文学层面的任何潮流或趋势。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"Why did Waterstones shops retire PRH books to their relevant sections?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make them easily noticeable."},{"key":"B","text":"To comply with PRH's requirement."},{"key":"C","text":"To respond to PRH's business move."},{"key":"D","text":"To arrange them in a systematic way."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"为什么Waterstones书店将PRH的书撤回到其相应的区域?","choicesZh":{"A":"使它们容易被注意到。","B":"遵守PRH的要求。","C":"回应PRH的商业举措。","D":"以系统化的方式排列它们。"},"analysis":{"type":"Why did Waterstones shops retire PRH books to their relevant sections?问的是一个原文已发生的具体动作的原因——客观可查、非主观推理。","parse":"一般过去时疑问句，主语 Waterstones shops，谓语 retire，宾语 PRH books，to + 地点。无嵌套从句、无陷阱。","locateEn":"The problem began late last year, when PRH confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones \"at a very significant level\". The trade magazine The Bookseller reported that Waterstones branch managers were being told to remove PRH books from prominent areas such as tables, display spaces and windows, and were \"quietly retiring them to their relevant sections\".","locateZh":"事情始于去年年底，当时 PRH 确认对 Waterstones 设置了\"非常高水平\"的信用额度。行业杂志《书商》报道说，Waterstones 各分店经理被告知把 PRH 的书从桌台、展位、橱窗等显眼位置撤下，\"悄悄地把它们放回各自相应的图书分区\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"To make them easily noticeable 说撤书是为\"让它们更容易被注意\"——但原文明白说是把书从 prominent areas such as tables, display spaces and windows 撤下，恰恰是\"让它们不再显眼\"，与选项语义相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"To comply with PRH's requirement 说撤书是\"遵从 PRH 的要求\"——但原文中要求撤书的是 Waterstones branch managers were being told，下令方是 Waterstones 自己（管理层），不是 PRH；PRH 只是设了\"信用额度\"，从未要求 Waterstones 撤书。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求选项把\"PRH 商业动作 → Waterstones 回应\"完整体现；C 项同时具备 business move（指 PRH 设限额）和 respond（指 Waterstones 撤书）两个核心要素，与预判一一对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"PRH confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones","opt":"To respond to PRH's business move"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"To arrange them in a systematic way 把撤书包装成\"按系统化方式排列\"——这是把一个商业反制动作美化成\"普通整理工作\"；原文用 quietly retiring（悄悄退架）和\"显眼位置撤下\"等措辞，明确是商业立场，不是日常整理。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"What message does the spokesperson for Waterstones seem to convey?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Their customers remain loyal."},{"key":"B","text":"The credit limit will be removed."},{"key":"C","text":"Their stock is underestimated."},{"key":"D","text":"The book market is rather slack."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Waterstones的发言人似乎传达了什么信息?","choicesZh":{"A":"他们的顾客保持忠诚。","B":"信用额度将被取消。","C":"他们的库存被低估了。","D":"图书市场相当疲软。"},"analysis":{"type":"What message does the spokesperson for Waterstones seem to convey? 含 seem to convey，是典型的\"话里的言外之意\"——属于推断题。","parse":"What 引导特殊疑问句，message 作宾语前置；定语从句 the spokesperson for Waterstones seem to convey 修饰 message。基础句式，不构成阅读障碍。","locateEn":"We are not boycotting PRH titles but we are doing our utmost to ensure that availability for customers remains good despite the lower overall levels of stock. We are hopeful with our shops now open again that normality will return and that we will be allowed to buy appropriately. Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.","locateZh":"我们没有抵制 PRH 的书，而是在尽全力确保即便整体库存下降、顾客的购书可得性仍然良好。我们希望随着各店重新开门，一切恢复正常，能够正常进货。可以肯定的是，我们的店里异常繁忙——5 月当月之书的销量超过了自 2018 年以来的任何一个月。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"发言人不直接谈顾客，而通过销量来谈顾客——把销量\"超过 2018 年以来任何一月\"换算成消费者评价，结论只能是\"顾客没走、还很忠实\"，与预判一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"our shops are exceptionally busy. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018","opt":"Their customers remain loyal"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The credit limit will be removed 把发言人对\"恢复正常\"的希望直接说成\"信用额度将被取消\"——原文只说 hopeful…that normality will return 是希望，未来事件不确定；hopeful 远不等于 will be removed。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Their stock is underestimated 说\"他们的库存被低估\"——但原文明确承认 the lower overall levels of stock，是\"整体库存确实变低\"，与\"被低估\"语义完全相反；underestimated 还把\"客观少\"歪曲成\"被主观看轻\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The book market is rather slack 说\"图书市场相当萧条\"——原文恰恰强调店里 exceptionally busy、销量 surpassed any month since 2018，是市场红火的证据；D 项把\"红火\"反成\"萧条\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"What can be one consequence of the current dispute?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably."},{"key":"B","text":"Lesser-known PRH writers become the target of criticism."},{"key":"C","text":"Waterstones staff hesitate to promote big-name authors' books."},{"key":"D","text":"Waterstones branches suffer a severe reduction in revenue."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"当前争端可能带来的后果是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"PRH中等知名度作家的书籍销量大幅下降。","B":"不太知名的PRH作家成为批评的对象。","C":"Waterstones的员工对推广知名作家的书籍犹豫不决。","D":"Waterstones的分店收入严重减少。"},"analysis":{"type":"What can be one consequence of the current dispute? 问的是文中明示的一种后果——文章既然把这场争端铺开了讲，必然会客观点出某些受损方，属于细节题。","parse":"情态动词 can 表示\"可能存在的一种\"——暗示原文给的不止一个后果，问其中之一。主干结构简单。","locateEn":"Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.","locateZh":"PRH 的大牌作者可能会受一点损失，但真正难熬的是那些中层作者——他们平时就靠 Waterstones 店员对推介小众作家书籍的热情，他们会盼着这场争端尽快结束。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的\"中层作者销量下滑\"在 A 项里完整呈现：主体（mid-list PRH writers）= 中层作者；后果（sales fall off considerably）= 销量明显下滑——两者一一对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books","opt":"Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Lesser-known PRH writers become the target of criticism 说不知名作者\"成了被批评的对象\"——原文从未提及任何对作者的批评；他们只是失去推介机会，不是被批评。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Waterstones staff hesitate to promote big-name authors' books 把推介对象错配为\"大牌作者\"——原文 promoting books by lesser-known writers 写得很清楚：店员推介的是知名度不高的作家的书，不是大牌。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Waterstones branches suffer a severe reduction in revenue 说 Waterstones 分店\"营收严重下降\"——但原文 our shops are exceptionally busy 还在强调店内极忙，全文也从未提 Waterstones 营收下降；选项把受损主体从作者偷偷换成了书店。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following statements best represents Lownie's view?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Small publishers ought to stick together."},{"key":"B","text":"Big publishers will lose their dominance."},{"key":"C","text":"The publishing industry is having a hard time."},{"key":"D","text":"The merger of publishers is a worrying trend."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"以下哪项陈述最能代表Lownie的观点?","choicesZh":{"A":"小型出版商应该团结一致。","B":"大型出版商将失去其主导地位。","C":"出版业正经历艰难时期。","D":"出版商的合并是一个令人担忧的趋势。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following statements best represents Lownie's view? 用 best represents——需要在四个改写句中挑\"最贴合\"Lownie 整段话主旨的一项，属于一步推断。","parse":"Which of the following statements 主语前置，best represents 谓语，宾语 Lownie's view。结构清晰，注意 best 提示\"四个里最贴合\"，不是\"绝对正确\"。","locateEn":"\"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power,\" says literary agent Andrew Lownie. \"The publishing industry talks about diversity in terms of authors and staff but it also needs a plurality of ways of delivering intellectual contact, choice and different voices. After all, many of the most interesting books in recent years have come from small publishers.\"","locateZh":"\"这一切都是权力集中这一更大趋势的一部分，\"文学经纪人 Andrew Lownie 说。\"出版业谈作者与员工的多样性，但它同样需要传递思想交流、选择与不同声音的多种渠道。毕竟，近年最有意思的许多书都来自小出版社。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Small publishers ought to stick together 说\"小出版社应该团结起来\"——原文 Lownie 只是举小出版社作为\"有趣书的来源\"佐证多元价值，并未呼吁小出版社团结或联合。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Big publishers will lose their dominance 说\"大出版商将失去其主导地位\"——但 Lownie 的核心担忧恰恰是大出版商通过合并\"权力越来越集中\"，地位会更强而非削弱；选项与他的判断方向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The publishing industry is having a hard time 把 Lownie 的具体担忧（合并/集中化）泛化为\"整个出版业正经历艰难时期\"——他没有说出版业整体困境，只针对集中化趋势和多元渠道的萎缩。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"首句\"权力集中\"定性 + 中段\"需要多元\" + 尾句\"小出版社实绩\"——共同指向\"合并这一趋势令人担忧\"，正与 D 项语义完全对齐。","pairs":[{"orig":"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power","opt":"The merger of publishers is a worrying trend"},{"orig":"After all, many of the most interesting books in recent years have come from small publishers","opt":"The merger of publishers is a worrying trend"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Scientific papers are the recordkeepers of progress in research. Each year researchers publish millions of papers in more than 30,000 journals. The scientific community measures the quality of those papers in a number of ways, including the perceived quality of the journal (as reflected by the title's impact factor) and the number of citations a specific paper accumulates. The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"Citation cartels, where journals, authors, and institutions conspire to inflate citation numbers, have existed for a long time. In 2016, researchers developed an algorithm to recognize suspicious citation patterns, including groups of authors that disproportionately cite one another and groups of journals that cite each other frequently to increase the impact factors of their publications. Recently, another expression of this predatory behavior has emerged: so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"The advent of electronic publishing and authors' need to find outlets for their papers resulted in thousands of new journals. The birth of predatory journals wasn't far behind. These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers. In some instances, there is absolutely no relationship between the content of the article and the citations. The peculiar part is that the journal that the editor is supposedly working for is not profiting at all—it is just providing citations to other journals. Such practices can lead an article to accrue more than 150 citations in the same year that it was published."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"How insidious is this type of citation manipulation? In one example, an individual—acting as author, editor, and consultant—was able to use at least 15 journals as citation providers to articles published by five scientists at three universities. The problem is rampant in Scopus, a citation database, which includes a high number of the new \"international\" journals. In fact, a listing in Scopus seems to be a criterion to be targeted in this type of citation manipulation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice. Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year. And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, the careers of scientists can be determined by______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"how many citations their works contain."},{"key":"B","text":"how many times their papers are cited."},{"key":"C","text":"the prestige of the people they work with."},{"key":"D","text":"the status they have in scientific circles."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,科学家的职业生涯可能由______决定","choicesZh":{"A":"他们的著作包含多少条引用","B":"他们的论文被引用多少次","C":"与他们合作的人的声望","D":"他们在科学界的地位"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to Paragraph 1, the careers of scientists can be determined by 是 '根据某段'+ 待补全陈述句，问段内的具体事实归因，没有 infer/imply 等推断信号。","parse":"题干 the careers of scientists can be determined by______ 是一个待补全的被动结构，主语 careers of scientists、谓语 can be determined by，by 后面缺宾语就是要选的内容；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers.","locateZh":"科学家的职业生涯和其所在机构的声誉，取决于他们所发表论文的数量和声望，但更取决于这些论文所吸引到的引用。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 how many citations their works contain 说的是 '论文里包含多少处引用'（即作者引了多少别人），而原文强调 citations attracted by these papers 是 '被多少人引用'，方向正好相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 how many times their papers are cited 与预判 '论文被引用了多少次' 字面与语义一一对应，且对应的是定位句被 'but even more so' 强调的那一项，是正确答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"the citations attracted by these papers","opt":"how many times their papers are cited"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 the prestige of the people they work with 说 '一起共事者的声望'，但原文 the number and prestige of the papers they produce 中的 prestige 修饰的是 papers（论文），而非合作者。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 the status they have in scientific circles 谈 '其在学界的个人地位'，原文从未把 status/standing 作为决定要素列出，且 reputation of their institutions 谈的是机构声誉而非个人地位。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"The support service consultancies tend to______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recommend journals to their clients."},{"key":"B","text":"list citation patterns for their clients."},{"key":"C","text":"ask authors to include extra citations."},{"key":"D","text":"advise contributors to cite each other."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"支持服务咨询机构往往会______","choicesZh":{"A":"向客户推荐期刊","B":"为客户列出引用模式","C":"要求作者加入额外的引用","D":"建议投稿人相互引用"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The support service consultancies tend to______ 锁定特定对象问其常做的事，是典型 'A 通常做 B' 型细节题。","parse":"题干 The support service consultancies tend to______ 主语是 The support service consultancies，谓语是 tend to + 动词原形，所选 A/B/C/D 都是动词原形短语，直接补在 to 后面即可；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Recently, another expression of this predatory behavior has emerged: so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles.","locateZh":"最近，这种掠夺性行为又出现了一种新形式——所谓的 'support service 咨询机构'，它们为个人作者和期刊提供语言及其他编辑支持，有时会建议投稿人为自己的文章添加若干引用。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 recommend journals to their clients 说 '向客户推荐期刊'，但定位句只说 advise contributors to add citations，没提推荐期刊一事。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 list citation patterns for their clients 说 '为客户列出引用模式'，可定位句的动词是 advise to add，不是 list；citation patterns 也只在前文 suspicious citation patterns 由 2016 年算法识别出现，与 support service consultancies 无关。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 ask authors to include extra citations 与预判 '让作者加引用' 字面与语义完全对应，是正确答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles","opt":"ask authors to include extra citations"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 advise contributors to cite each other 把动作扭曲成 '让投稿人之间互相引用'，可定位句只说 add citations to their articles，并未规定要互引；互引描述的是 groups of authors that disproportionately cite one another，属另一主体。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The function of the \"milk cow\" journals is to______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"boost citation counts for certain authors."},{"key":"B","text":"help scholars publish articles at low cost."},{"key":"C","text":"instruct first-time contributors in citation."},{"key":"D","text":"increase the readership of new journals."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"奶牛期刊的作用是______","choicesZh":{"A":"提高某些作者的引用次数","B":"帮助学者以低成本发表文章","C":"指导首次投稿人进行引用","D":"增加新期刊的读者数量"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The function of the \"milk cow\" journals is to______ 锁定文中一个具体对象问其功能，答案应能逐字回溯到原文一句话。","parse":"题干 The function of the \"milk cow\" journals is to______ 主干为 The function ... is to + 动词原形，是典型的功能定义句式；选项均以动词原形开头，直接补在 to 后面；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers. In some instances, there is absolutely no relationship between the content of the article and the citations.","locateZh":"这些期刊可以充当 '奶牛'：一期里每一篇文章都可能引用某一篇特定的论文或一组论文。在某些情形下，文章的内容与所添加的引用之间毫无关系。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 boost citation counts for certain authors 既对应 'cite a specific paper' 的机制，又对应 'accrue more than 150 citations' 的后果，是唯一同时覆盖原文机制 + 结果的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers","opt":"boost citation counts for certain authors"},{"orig":"Such practices can lead an article to accrue more than 150 citations in the same year that it was published","opt":"boost citation counts for certain authors"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 help scholars publish articles at low cost 说 '帮学者低成本发表文章'，原文 P3 从头到尾没提 cost/fee/charge 等任何成本词，纯属增项。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 instruct first-time contributors in citation 说 '指导首次投稿人如何引用'，原文 P3 完全没出现 first-time / instruct / teach 等动词，与 milk cow 期刊的 '互引刷量' 功能毫无关系。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 increase the readership of new journals 说 '扩大新期刊读者群'，原文重点在 'citations'（引用次数）而非 'readership'（读者群），且 the journal that the editor is supposedly working for is not profiting at all 直接否认其期刊本身受益。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"What can be learned about Scopus from the last two paragraphs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It fosters competition among citation providers."},{"key":"B","text":"It has the capability to identify suspicious citations."},{"key":"C","text":"It hinders the growth of \"international\" journals."},{"key":"D","text":"It is established to prevent citation manipulation."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从最后两段可以了解到Scopus的什么信息?","choicesZh":{"A":"它促进了引用提供者之间的竞争","B":"它有能力识别可疑引用","C":"它阻碍了国际期刊的发展","D":"它是为防止引用操纵而建立的"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What can be learned about Scopus from the last two paragraphs? 用 learned 而非 inferred/implied，问的是 '段内交代了关于 X 的什么事实'，仍是细节题。","parse":"题干 What can be learned about Scopus from the last two paragraphs? 是 What 引导的特殊疑问句，about Scopus 是话题、from the last two paragraphs 是范围状语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice.","locateZh":"Scopus 自己就拥有检测这一不端行为所需的全部数据。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 It fosters competition among citation providers 说 'Scopus 促进引用提供者间的竞争'，原文 P4P5 全无 foster、competition、competitors 等词，且 Scopus 在文中是被 '攻陷' 的角色，谈不上 'foster competition'。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 It has the capability to identify suspicious citations 把 '有数据可检测不端' 客观还原为 '有能力识别可疑引用'，与预判一致，是正确答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice","opt":"It has the capability to identify suspicious citations"},{"orig":"Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year","opt":"It has the capability to identify suspicious citations"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 It hinders the growth of \"international\" journals 说 'Scopus 阻碍国际期刊成长'，原文 The problem is rampant in Scopus 恰恰相反——这些 'international' 期刊被收入 Scopus 后引用操纵更严重，Scopus 在客观上是其温床而非阻碍。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 It is established to prevent citation manipulation 说 'Scopus 被建立来防止引用操纵'，但原文只说它 has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice，谈的是 '具备能力'，不是 '设立宗旨'；而且 P4 表明它实际上是引用操纵的高发地，与 'established to prevent' 的语义相悖。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"What should an author do to deal with citation manipulators?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take legal action."},{"key":"B","text":"Demand an apology."},{"key":"C","text":"Seek professional advice."},{"key":"D","text":"Reveal their misconduct."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者应该如何应对引用操纵者?","choicesZh":{"A":"采取法律行动","B":"要求道歉","C":"寻求专业建议","D":"揭露他们的不当行为"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What should an author do to deal with citation manipulators? 直接问 '应该做什么'，答案需逐字回溯到原文一句应对建议。","parse":"题干 What should an author do to deal with citation manipulators? 主干是 What should an author do，to deal with citation manipulators 是目的状语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal.","locateZh":"对于希望远离引用卡特尔活动的作者来说：当编辑、审稿人或支持服务机构要求你添加不当引用时，不要照办，并要把该请求上报给所投期刊。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Take legal action 说 '诉诸法律'，原文只说向所投期刊举报（report the request to the journal），属于学术规范处理而非法律程序，跨越了原文边界。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Demand an apology 说 '要求一份道歉'，原文 P5 的建议是 'do not oblige and do report'，完全没提 apologize/apology，纯属无中生有。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Seek professional advice 说 '寻求专业建议'，可原文给的建议是作者本人直接拒绝并举报，没让作者再去咨询他人；且 so-called support service consultancies 反而是文中给作者添麻烦的角色，'professional advice' 在本文语境下是负面来源。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Reveal their misconduct 与预判 '举报/上报/披露' 对应；'do not oblige' 是消极动作（拒绝照办），而四选项里只有 D 抓住了积极动作（公开/上报），故 D 是正确答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"do report the request to the journal","opt":"Reveal their misconduct"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"ordering","title":"Section II Part B 段落排序","directions":"Directions: The following paragraphs are given in a wrong order. For questions 41 -45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-H and filling them into the numbered boxes. Paragraphs A, E, and H have been correctly placed. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"A","text":"Last year marked the 150th anniversary of a series of Yellowstone photographs by the renowned landscape photographer William Henry Jackson. Jackson snapped the first-ever shots of iconic landmarks such as the Tetons, Old Faithful and the Colorado Rockies on a late 19th-century expedition through the Yellowstone Basin, conducted by the head of the U.S. Geological and Geographical Survey of the Territories, Ferdinand V. Hayden. The team included a meteorologist, a zoologist, a mineralogist, and an agricultural statistician."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"B","text":"Two centuries ago, the idea of preserving nature, rather than exploiting it, was a novel one to many US settlers. One of the turning points in public support for land conservation efforts—and recognizing the magnificence of the Yellowstone region in particular—came in the form of vivid photographs."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"C","text":"As an effective Washington operator, Hayden sensed that he could capitalize on the expedition's stunning visuals. He asked Jackson to print out large copies and distributed them, along with reproductions of Moran's paintings, to each member of Congress. \"The visualization, particularly those photographs, really hit home that this is something that has to be protected,\" says Alicia Murphy, Yellowstone's park historian."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"D","text":"Throughout the trip, Jackson juggled multiple cameras and plate sizes using the collodion process that involved coating the plates with a chemical mixture, exposing them and developing the resulting images with a portable darkroom. The crude technique required educated guesses on exposure times, and involved heavy, awkward equipment—several men had to assist in its transportation. Despite these challenges, Jackson captured dozens of striking photos, ranging from majestic images like his now-famous snapshot of Old Faithful, to casual portraits of expedition members at the camp. While veterans of previous expeditions had written at length about stunning sights, these vivid photographs were another thing entirely."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"E","text":"The journey officially began in Ogden, Utah, on June 8, 1871. Over nearly four months, dozens of men made their way on horseback into Montana and traversed along the Yellowstone River and around Yellowstone Lake. That fall, they concluded the survey in Fort Bridger, Wyoming."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"F","text":"Though Native Americans (and later miners and fur trappers) had long recognized the area's riches, most Americans did not. That's why Hayden's expedition aimed to produce a fuller understanding of the Yellowstone River region, from its hot springs and waterfalls to its variety of flora and fauna. In addition to the entourage of scientists, the team also included artists: Painter Thomas Moran and photographer Jackson were charged with capturing this astounding natural beauty and sharing it with the world."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"G","text":"The bill proved largely popular and sailed through Congress with large majorities in favor. In quick succession, the Senate and House passed legislation protecting Yellowstone in early 1872. That March, President Ulysses S. Grant signed an act into law that established Yellowstone as the world's first national park. While some locals opposed the designation, the decision was largely accepted—and Jackson's photos played a key role in the fight to protect the area. \"I don't believe that the legal protection would have happened in the time frame that it did without those images,\" says Heather Hansen, journalist and author of Prophets and Moguls, Rangers and Rogues, Bison and Bears: 100 Years of the National Park Service."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"H","text":"Perhaps most importantly, these images provided documentary evidence that later made its way to government officials. Weeks after completing the expedition, Hayden collected his team's observations into an extensive report aimed at convincing senators and representatives, along with colleagues at government agencies like the Department of the Interior, that Yellowstone ought to be preserved."}],"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Last year marked the 150th anniversary of a series of Yellowstone photographs by the renowned landscape photographer William Henry Jackson. Jackson snapped the first-ever shots of iconic landmarks such as the Tetons, Old Faithful and the Colorado Rockies on a late 19th-century expedition through the Yellowstone Basin, conducted by the head of the U.S. Geological and Geographical Survey of the Territories, Ferdinand V. Hayden. The team included a meteorologist, a zoologist, a mineralogist, and an agricultural statistician."},{"key":"B","text":"Two centuries ago, the idea of preserving nature, rather than exploiting it, was a novel one to many US settlers. One of the turning points in public support for land conservation efforts—and recognizing the magnificence of the Yellowstone region in particular—came in the form of vivid photographs."},{"key":"C","text":"As an effective Washington operator, Hayden sensed that he could capitalize on the expedition's stunning visuals. He asked Jackson to print out large copies and distributed them, along with reproductions of Moran's paintings, to each member of Congress. \"The visualization, particularly those photographs, really hit home that this is something that has to be protected,\" says Alicia Murphy, Yellowstone's park historian."},{"key":"D","text":"Throughout the trip, Jackson juggled multiple cameras and plate sizes using the collodion process that involved coating the plates with a chemical mixture, exposing them and developing the resulting images with a portable darkroom. The crude technique required educated guesses on exposure times, and involved heavy, awkward equipment—several men had to assist in its transportation. Despite these challenges, Jackson captured dozens of striking photos, ranging from majestic images like his now-famous snapshot of Old Faithful, to casual portraits of expedition members at the camp. While veterans of previous expeditions had written at length about stunning sights, these vivid photographs were another thing entirely."},{"key":"E","text":"The journey officially began in Ogden, Utah, on June 8, 1871. Over nearly four months, dozens of men made their way on horseback into Montana and traversed along the Yellowstone River and around Yellowstone Lake. That fall, they concluded the survey in Fort Bridger, Wyoming."},{"key":"F","text":"Though Native Americans (and later miners and fur trappers) had long recognized the area's riches, most Americans did not. That's why Hayden's expedition aimed to produce a fuller understanding of the Yellowstone River region, from its hot springs and waterfalls to its variety of flora and fauna. In addition to the entourage of scientists, the team also included artists: Painter Thomas Moran and photographer Jackson were charged with capturing this astounding natural beauty and sharing it with the world."},{"key":"G","text":"The bill proved largely popular and sailed through Congress with large majorities in favor. In quick succession, the Senate and House passed legislation protecting Yellowstone in early 1872. That March, President Ulysses S. Grant signed an act into law that established Yellowstone as the world's first national park. While some locals opposed the designation, the decision was largely accepted—and Jackson's photos played a key role in the fight to protect the area. \"I don't believe that the legal protection would have happened in the time frame that it did without those images,\" says Heather Hansen, journalist and author of Prophets and Moguls, Rangers and Rogues, Bison and Bears: 100 Years of the National Park Service."},{"key":"H","text":"Perhaps most importantly, these images provided documentary evidence that later made its way to government officials. Weeks after completing the expedition, Hayden collected his team's observations into an extensive report aimed at convincing senators and representatives, along with colleagues at government agencies like the Department of the Interior, that Yellowstone ought to be preserved."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"B"},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F"},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"D"},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C"},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G"}],"order":["B","A","F","E","D","H","C","G"],"fixed":{"1":"A","3":"E","5":"H"},"chain":"41. → A → 42. → E → 43. → H → 44. → 45.","orderChain":"正确顺序 41 B → 预给 A → 42 F → 预给 E → 43 D → 预给 H → 44 C → 45 G","seams":["【引出后一段】 段 A 语义承接：B 抛出「转折来自照片」，A 紧接着把这组照片具体化为 Jackson 所拍 。B 段尾只说 came in the form of vivid photographs，没说是谁的照片；given A 开头 a series of Yellowstone photographs by ... William Henry Jackson 正是对这「照片」的具体交代。无显式回指词，靠「抽象→具体」的内容顺承（弱锚），但方向与 given A 的钉死位置完全吻合。","【承接前一段】 段 A 词汇复现：F 复现 given A 的 Hayden 与 expedition，承接它去解释「这趟考察要干什么」 。given A 刚引入 a late 19th-century expedition through the Yellowstone Basin, conducted by the head of the U.S. Geological and Geographical Survey of the Territories, Ferdinand V. Hayden；42 位的 F 紧接着用 Hayden's expedition aimed to produce a fuller understanding 复现 Hayden、expedition 两个关键词，回答「这次考察的目的」。词汇链直接把 F 钉在 given A 之后。","【引出后一段】 段 E 指代衔接：F 交代完考察目的与人员，given E 用 The journey 定指承接，开始讲它何时启程 。F 把这趟考察是什么、带了谁说清后，given E 段首 The journey officially began 用定冠词 The journey 特指 F 里那次 Hayden's expedition，顺势进入「何时何地启程」。F 正好夹在 given A 与 given E 之间，两侧接缝都成立。","【承接前一段】 段 E 指代衔接：D 段首 the trip 定指回指 given E 刚讲完的那趟为期数月的旅程 。given E 把这趟旅程的时间路线交代完（Over nearly four months 的骑马行程）；43 位 D 段首 Throughout the trip 用 the trip 定指回指这趟旅程，顺势讲「途中怎么拍照」。the trip 必须有先行词，E 正是那个先行词所在段，故 D 紧接 given E。","【承接前一段】 段 H 词汇复现：H 写 Hayden 编报告要游说议员，C 写他具体怎么游说——把照片分发给每位议员 。given H 说 Hayden aimed at convincing senators and representatives；44 位 C 段首的 He 即 Hayden，distributed them ... to each member of Congress 正是对「如何说服议员」的具体落实，member of Congress 与 senators and representatives 同指国会，构成复现与顺承。","【引出后一段】 段 G 语义承接：C 写照片打动议员「必须保护」，G 紧接着写议案果然在国会顺利通过 。C 段尾 this is something that has to be protected 把议员被打动、倾向保护的氛围烘托出来；G 段首 The bill proved largely popular and sailed through Congress 的 The bill 正是这股保护意愿落成的议案，「被打动 → 法案顺利通过」逻辑顺承，C 紧接 given H、后接 G。","【承接前一段】 段 H 词汇复现：H 写 Hayden 力劝议员「应当保护」，G 写国会果真立法保护，是「劝说→结果」顺承 。given H 段尾 convincing senators and representatives ... that Yellowstone ought to be preserved，G 段则给出结果 passed legislation protecting Yellowstone、established Yellowstone as the world's first national park。senators/representatives 与 Senate/House、preserved 与 protecting 形成词汇复现链，且逻辑是「游说 → 通过」的因果顺承，G 收尾全文。"]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"There has been some exploration around the use of artificial intelligence (AI) in digital marketing. For example, AI can be used to analyse what type of advertising content or copy would be appropriate to \"speak\" to a specific target customer group by revealing information about trends and preferences through the analysis of big data. (46) AI can also be used to identify the lifestyle choices of customers regarding their hobbies, favourite celebrities, and fashions to provide unique content in marketing messages put out through social media. At the same time AI can also be used to generate content for social media posts and chat sites."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"The main disadvantage of using AI to respond to customers is that there are concerns about trusting personal interactions to machines, which could lead not only to the subsequent loss of interpersonal connections, but also to a decrease in marketing personnel. (47) Some believe that AI is negatively impacting on the marketer's role by reducing creativity and removing jobs, but they are aware that it is a way of reducing costs and creating new information. By allowing AI to develop content some brand marketers may find that they are losing control over the brand narrative. (48) Algorithms used to simulate human interactions are creating many of these concerns, especially as no-one is quite sure what the outcomes of using AI to interact with customers will be."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"For AI to be successful, data needs to be accessible, but the use of personal data is becoming more regulated and the automated sharing of data is becoming more difficult. (49) If customers are not willing to share data, AI will be starved of essential information and will not be able to function effectively or employ machine learning to improve its marketing content and communication. Therefore, unless customers are prepared to sign release agreements, the use of AI may become somewhat restricted in the future. Not only can AI help to create the marketing content, but it can also provide a non-intrusive way of delivering the content to the target customers. Data can be gathered on where the customer can be engaged, such as location, devices used, website interactions, and sites visited, to display marketing messages in appropriate forms, including emails, social media posts, pop-up advertisements, and banners at an appropriate frequency. (50) The non-intrusive delivery of the marketing messages in a way that is sensitive to the needs of target customers is one of the critical challenges to the digital marketer."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"AI can also be used to identify the lifestyle choices of customers regarding their hobbies, favourite celebrities, and fashions to provide unique content in marketing messages put out through social media.","refZh":"人工智能还可以用来识别客户在爱好、喜爱的名人和时尚潮流等方面的生活方式选择，从而为通过社交媒体发布的营销信息提供独特的内容。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"AI can also be used to identify the lifestyle choices of customers","lit":"人工智能还能被用来识别客户的生活方式选择","role":"（主干（被动）+ 不定式宾语）","note":"难点： 被动 be used to 转主动 AI can also be used to identify the lifestyle choices of customers 是 be used to do 被动结构，直译「AI 被用来…」有翻译腔，汉化时转成主动「AI 还可以用来…／还能用来…」更自然。lifestyle choices 直译「生活方式选择」即可，指客户在生活方式上的偏好。"},{"en":"regarding their hobbies, favourite celebrities, and fashions","lit":"关于他们的爱好、喜爱的名人和时尚","role":"（介词短语作定语（regarding=关于））","note":"难点： regarding 译「在…方面」 regarding 是介词，意为「关于、就…而言」，这里 regarding their hobbies, favourite celebrities, and fashions 修饰前面的 lifestyle choices，说明在哪些方面的选择。汉化为「在爱好、喜爱的名人和时尚（潮流）等方面」，提到所修饰的名词前更顺。celebrities 译「名人」，fashions 此处指时尚潮流。"},{"en":"to provide unique content in marketing messages","lit":"以便在营销信息中提供独特的内容","role":"（不定式作目的状语）","note":"难点： 目的状语 to provide 这个 to provide 是「识别客户偏好」的目的，译「从而／以便提供…」。content 按全文统一译「内容」，unique 译「独特的」，marketing messages 译「营销信息」。"},{"en":"put out through social media.","lit":"通过社交媒体发布的","role":"（过去分词短语作后置定语（修饰 marketing messages））","note":"难点： put out 熟词僻义+后置定语 put out 在此不是「熄灭、生气」，而是「发布、推出」之义，是熟词僻义；它以过去分词 put（put 三态同形）作后置定语修饰 marketing messages，即「（通过社交媒体）发布出去的营销信息」。汉化时把这个后置定语前移到 marketing messages 之前：「通过社交媒体发布的营销信息」。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"Some believe that AI is negatively impacting on the marketer's role by reducing creativity and removing jobs, but they are aware that it is a way of reducing costs and creating new information.","refZh":"一些人认为，人工智能削弱了创造力、减少了工作岗位，正在对营销人员的作用产生负面影响，但他们也清楚，它是一种降低成本、创造新信息的途径。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Some believe that AI is negatively impacting on the marketer's role","lit":"一些人认为人工智能正在对营销人员的角色产生负面影响","role":"（主句 + that 宾语从句）","note":"难点： impact on 译「对…产生影响」 impact on 是「对…产生影响、冲击」，negatively impacting on 即「产生负面影响」。Some 在句首指「一些人／有些人」。marketer 指「营销人员／营销者」，role 指「角色、作用」。"},{"en":"by reducing creativity and removing jobs,","lit":"通过减少创造力和削减工作岗位","role":"（by + 动名词，方式状语）","note":"难点： by doing 译「（通过）使…」 by reducing… and removing… 说明 AI 是「怎样」产生负面影响的，是方式状语。汉化时可不必死译「通过」，译成「（即）削弱创造力、减少（删减）工作岗位」并入上句更顺。removing jobs 指「裁撤岗位、减少工作机会」。"},{"en":"but they are aware that it is a way of reducing costs and creating new information.","lit":"但他们意识到它是一种降低成本和创造新信息的方式","role":"（but 引导的转折分句 + that 宾语从句）","note":"难点： they 与 it 的指代还原 they 回指句首的 Some（那些人），译「他们」即可；it 指代前文的 AI，可译「它」或回填「人工智能」。are aware that 译「意识到、清楚」。a way of doing 译「一种…的方式／途径」。这一分句与前面 but 转折，构成「虽认为有害，但也清楚有利」的对照。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"Algorithms used to simulate human interactions are creating many of these concerns, especially as no-one is quite sure what the outcomes of using AI to interact with customers will be.","refZh":"用来模拟人际互动的算法正在引发许多这样的担忧，尤其是因为没有人能十分确定，使用人工智能与客户互动究竟会带来什么样的结果。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Algorithms used to simulate human interactions","lit":"用来模拟人际互动的算法","role":"（主语 + used to do 过去分词后置定语）","note":"难点： used to 此处是「被用来」非「过去常常」 陷阱点：used to 在此不是「过去常常做某事」，而是过去分词短语 used to simulate…（被用来模拟…）作后置定语修饰 Algorithms。判断依据：句子主干谓语是后面的 are creating，所以这里的 used 不是谓语，只能是定语。译「用来模拟人际互动的算法」，把定语前移。simulate human interactions 指「模拟人与人之间的互动」。"},{"en":"are creating many of these concerns,","lit":"正在引发许多这样的担忧","role":"（主干谓语 + 宾语）","note":"难点： these concerns 回指上文担忧 these concerns 是跨句指代，须回第 2 段上文还原：指前文 there are concerns about trusting personal interactions to machines 及由此带来的人际连接流失、营销人员减少、品牌叙事失控等顾虑。翻译时译「这些（这样的）担忧／顾虑」即可，无须展开，但理解上要知道它承接上文。are creating 译「正在引发／造成」，比直译「创造」更贴 concerns。"},{"en":"especially as no-one is quite sure","lit":"尤其是因为没有人十分确定","role":"（as 引导原因状语从句（especially 强调））","note":"难点： as 译「因为」 as 在此是从属连词，表原因，译「因为、由于」，不是「作为／当」。especially as 译「尤其是因为」。no-one is quite sure 译「没有人十分确定／说得准」，quite 修饰 sure，是「相当、十分」。"},{"en":"what the outcomes of using AI to interact with customers will be.","lit":"使用人工智能与客户互动的结果将会是什么","role":"（what 引导的宾语从句（作 sure 的宾语））","note":"难点： what…will be 表语从句倒装还原 这是 sure 后接的宾语从句，正常语序是 the outcomes of using AI… will be what。理解时把 what 还原到 will be 后：「使用 AI 与客户互动的结果会是什么」。outcomes 译「结果、后果」，of using AI to interact with customers 是修饰 outcomes 的定语，译「使用 AI 与客户互动（所产生）的结果」。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"If customers are not willing to share data, AI will be starved of essential information and will not be able to function effectively or employ machine learning to improve its marketing content and communication.","refZh":"如果客户不愿意分享数据，人工智能就会缺乏必不可少的信息，从而无法有效运作，也无法运用机器学习来改进其营销内容和沟通。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"If customers are not willing to share data,","lit":"如果客户不愿意分享数据","role":"（if 引导的条件状语从句）","note":"难点： if 条件从句前置 if 引导条件状语从句，译「如果／一旦」。be willing to do 译「愿意做」，not willing 即「不愿意」。share data 译「分享／共享数据」。汉语习惯把条件放句首，正好与原文同序，直接译即可。"},{"en":"AI will be starved of essential information","lit":"人工智能将被剥夺必要的信息","role":"（主句一（被动））","note":"难点： be starved of 熟词僻义 starve 本义「挨饿」，be starved of sth 是固定搭配，意为「极度缺乏、被剥夺（某物）」——这是熟词僻义陷阱，不能译「AI 会饿」。结合语境（缺数据则缺信息）译「AI 将缺乏／得不到必要的信息」。essential 译「必不可少的、必要的」。"},{"en":"and will not be able to function effectively","lit":"并且将无法有效运作","role":"（主句二（and 并列））","note":"难点： function 作动词「运作」 function 此处是动词「运转、发挥作用」，不是名词「功能」——又一处熟词僻义。be able to function effectively 译「能有效运作／正常发挥作用」，前加 not 即「无法有效运作」。"},{"en":"or employ machine learning to improve its marketing content and communication.","lit":"或运用机器学习来改进它的营销内容和沟通","role":"（or 并列谓语 + 不定式目的状语）","note":"难点： employ 译「运用」+ or 受前 not 统辖 employ 在此不是「雇佣（人）」，而是「运用、采用（方法）」，宾语是 machine learning（机器学习）。这个 or 与前面 will not be able to 共享否定，即「也无法运用机器学习……」。to improve 是目的状语，its 指代 AI，improve its marketing content and communication 译「改进其营销内容与沟通」。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"The non-intrusive delivery of the marketing messages in a way that is sensitive to the needs of target customers is one of the critical challenges to the digital marketer.","refZh":"如何以一种非侵扰、且顾及目标客户需求的方式投放营销信息，是数字营销人员面临的关键挑战之一。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The non-intrusive delivery of the marketing messages","lit":"营销信息的非侵扰式投放","role":"（主语核心（抽象名词 delivery））","note":"难点： 抽象名词 delivery 具体化为动作 delivery 是抽象名词（动词 deliver 的名词化），直译「投递、传送」偏硬，可具体化为动作「投放、传递、推送」。non-intrusive 译「非侵扰式的、不打扰（用户）的」，呼应前文 a non-intrusive way of delivering the content。整块译「以非侵扰的方式投放营销信息」，把名词 delivery 还原成动作「投放」，读来更顺。"},{"en":"in a way that is sensitive to the needs of target customers","lit":"以一种顾及目标客户需求的方式","role":"（方式状语 + that 定语从句（修饰 way））","note":"难点： be sensitive to 译「顾及/敏感于」 that is sensitive to… 是修饰 way 的定语从句。be sensitive to sth 不是「对…敏感（生理）」，在此指「体察、顾及、关照（某需求）」。in a way that is sensitive to the needs of target customers 译「以一种顾及／关照目标客户需求的方式」。target customers 译「目标客户」。"},{"en":"is one of the critical challenges to the digital marketer.","lit":"是数字营销人员面临的关键挑战之一","role":"（主干谓语 + 表语）","note":"难点： one of the…challenges 译「……之一」 句子真正的谓语是这个 is（前面一长串都是主语）。one of the critical challenges 译「关键挑战之一」，critical 译「关键的、至关重要的」。challenges to the digital marketer 中 to 表「对……而言」，译「数字营销人员面临的挑战」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: Write a notice to recruit a student for Prof. Smith’s research project on campus sports activities. Specify the duties and requirements of the job. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in the notice; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: Write a notice to recruit a student for Prof. Smith’s research project on campus sports activities. Specify the duties and requirements of the job. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in the notice; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Notice Prof. Smith is currently conducting a research project on campus sports activities and is now recruiting one student assistant. The chosen student will help design questionnaires, distribute them among students, and collect and record the data during the coming term. Applicants should be undergraduates who are interested in sports research, careful with numbers, and able to spare about five hours each week; a basic command of Excel is preferred. Those interested are welcome to send a short self-introduction to sports@campus.edu, or contact Li Ming for further details before June 20th. Li Ming","translation":"通知\nSmith 教授正在开展一项关于校园体育活动的研究项目，现招募一名学生助手。入选的学生将协助设计问卷、向同学发放问卷、并在下学期收集和录入数据。\n应聘者应为在读本科生，对体育研究有兴趣、对数据细致，并每周能抽出约五小时；会基本的 Excel 操作者优先。有意者欢迎在 6 月 20 日前将一份简短的自我介绍发送至 sports@campus.edu，或联系 Li Ming 了解更多信息。\nLi Ming","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"标题落文体","text":"【第 1 段】 标题落文体 。单独一行居中的「Notice」落实了 outline 第一块「居中标题」，让阅卷人一眼确认这是 a notice。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"事由接职责","text":"【第 2 段】 事由接职责 。用「Prof. Smith is currently conducting a research project…and is now recruiting one student assistant」套「点明发布事由」句架交代由头，再用「The chosen student will help design questionnaires, distribute them…and collect and record the data」并列列出 duties，落实第二块功能。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"要求接报名","text":"【第 3 段】 要求接报名 。「Applicants should be undergraduates who are…and able to spare about five hours each week」套「列任职要求」句架写 requirements；再以「Those interested are welcome to send…or contact Li Ming…before June 20th」给出报名方式与截止时间，使通知可操作。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"匿名落款","text":"【第 4 段】 匿名落款 。末行「Li Ming」落实署名块，严格遵守 use “Li Ming” instead，未出现真名。"}],"wordCount":93}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay based on the picture below. In your essay, you should 1) describe the picture briefly, 2) interpret the implied meaning, and 3) give your comments. Write your answer in 160-200 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay based on the picture below. In your essay, you should 1) describe the picture briefly, 2) interpret the implied meaning, and 3) give your comments. Write your answer in 160-200 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2023-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白线描的卡通风格的画作","width":"660","height":"661","local":"assets/writing/2023-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a lively dragon boat race is taking place on a river running through a village. Two boats full of rowers compete fiercely, while crowds on both banks and the arched bridge wave flags to cheer. In the corner, an elderly man smiles and says, \"How wonderful! The dragon boat race in our village is becoming more and more lively.\" Simple as it seems, the picture conveys a thought-provoking message: traditional folk customs are being revived and flourishing in the countryside. The dragon boat race, a time-honored custom, is not fading away but attracting growing enthusiasm from villagers of all ages. This mirrors a nationwide revival of traditional culture and the rising cultural confidence in recent years. From my perspective, such a phenomenon deserves our applause. On one hand, reviving traditional customs enriches people's spiritual lives and strengthens community bonds; on the other, it passes our cultural heritage down to younger generations. Therefore, we should take concrete steps to protect and promote these customs so that our splendid traditional culture can shine forever.","translation":"如漫画生动描绘的那样，一场热闹的龙舟赛正在一条穿村而过的河上进行。两艘坐满桨手的龙舟激烈竞渡，两岸和拱桥上的人群挥舞旗帜为之呐喊。角落里，一位老人含笑说道：“真好啊！咱们村的龙舟赛越来越热闹了。”\n画面看似简单，却传递出一个发人深省的信息：传统民俗正在乡村复兴并日益兴旺。龙舟赛这项历史悠久的习俗非但没有消亡，反而吸引着各年龄段村民日益高涨的热情。这折射出近年来全国范围内传统文化的复兴与文化自信的提升。\n在我看来，这一现象值得称赞。一方面，复兴传统民俗丰富了人们的精神生活、凝聚了社区情感；另一方面，它把我们的文化遗产传承给了年轻一代。因此，我们应当采取切实措施来保护和推广这些民俗，让我们灿烂的传统文化永放光彩。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"白描三句，客观点题","text":"【第 1 段】 白描三句，客观点题 。本段用起手式 As is vividly depicted in the cartoon 引出画面，随后一句写主体龙舟竞渡与两岸助威，末句译出对白 How wonderful! The dragon boat race in our village is becoming more and more lively，只描述不评价，落实了 describe the picture briefly。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"过渡挖寓意并联系现实","text":"【第 2 段】 过渡挖寓意并联系现实 。本段以 Simple as it seems 过渡，把画面拉向内涵，点出 traditional folk customs are being revived，再用 This mirrors a nationwide revival 联系现实趋势，完成了阅卷核心的 interpret the implied meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"表态、分层、给对策","text":"【第 3 段】 表态、分层、给对策 。本段先 From my perspective 亮明肯定态度，用 On one hand / on the other 分两层说价值，末句 Therefore, we should take concrete steps 给出对策收尾，正是 give your comments 所要求的评论。"}],"wordCount":179}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 C located · 2 A privately · 3 D combination · 4 C describe · 5 C such as · 6 A construction · 7 B faced · 8 B subjected · 9 A so that · 10 D meeting · 11 D As a result · 12 C exchange · 13 C as well as · 14 B influencing · 15 A aided · 16 B Indeed · 17 D stock up on · 18 A believed · 19 D although · 20 A ruins \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 B · 23 A · 24 C · 25 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 A · 27 D · 28 B · 29 C · 30 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 A · 32 C · 33 A · 34 A · 35 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 B · 37 C · 38 A · 39 B · 40 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落排序 Section II Part B 41=B → 预给A → 42=F → 预给E → 43=D → 预给H → 44=C → 45=G \n（逐题解析见 段落排序解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
